# Build and developer tools

Canonical guidance: `docs/engineering/cmake-python.md`. Version policy: `docs/engineering/VERSIONS.md`. Verification/playtest contract: `docs/VERIFICATION.md`.

CMake:
- target-scoped settings;
- explicit project source lists;
- immutable dependency revisions;
- keep GoogleTest test-only and godot-cpp GDExtension-only;
- do not make third-party code inherit project-wide `-Werror` accidentally.

Python:
- repository environment and pinned tooling;
- `pathlib`;
- explicit argv subprocess calls, cwd/environment and bounded timeout;
- one Godot playtest supervisor once `tools/play.py` exists;
- cleanup only processes owned by the current run.

Do not:
- use source GLOBs for project code;
- add a second SCons graph;
- use floating dependency branches;
- fetch dependencies unexpectedly during ordinary tests/playtests;
- use `shell=True`, `pkill godot` or infinite polling as convenience shortcuts;
- introduce Playwright/Chromium for the Godot client.
